<h2 id="the-power-of-simplicity">The Power of Simplicity</h2>

<p>Here’s what we learned:</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Agents are loops</strong>: just keep asking the model “what’s next?”</li>
  <li><strong>Tools are descriptions</strong>: the LLM chooses, you execute.</li>
  <li><strong>Context is precious</strong>: every message costs tokens and attention.</li>
  <li><strong>Emergent behavior is real</strong>: complex behavior arises from simple rules.</li>
</ol>

<p>The entire Nimbo agent is under 300 lines of Swift. Yet it can:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Navigate the file system.</li>
  <li>Read and modify files.</li>
  <li>Chain multiple operations together.</li>
  <li>Handle errors gracefully.</li>
</ul>

<p>That’s the power of building on top of a language model. You’re not coding every possibility; you’re creating a space where the model can think and act.</p>

